      "message": "The \"$?\" will be 0 if both commands were executed properly - the first one, `rm -f` should not really fail - we don\u0027t expect it. If it did the error will propagate to \"$?\" into our check. So far it is good.\nThe result of the next command after the `\u0026\u0026` clause depends on the `xargs` command exit status. The `xargs` can fail if the executed command fails, i.e. cp. So up to now it looks correct - If `cp` fails the `if` clause will fire so the check works fine. So to sum up, we don\u0027t need to group these with parenthesis, it would work as expected.",
